  "academic_insight": "In Low-density real photographs, YOLOv8n achieves near-exact counts because individuals are separated. In High and Extreme densities (>500 persons), YOLOv8n misses over 98% of heads due to occlusion, whereas CSRNet maps spatial density directly. Note that our 8-epoch CPU-calibrated CSRNet model still shows residual background over-prediction on Negative/Low scenes; full multi-epoch GPU training on all 3,109 NWPU-Crowd training images is required for production accuracy (published CSRNet benchmark MAE: 104.89)."
